#2.6 Major Neural Network Types
Connectionist AI relies on Artificial Neural Networks (ANNs), which model cognition using layers of interconnected processing units (artificial neurons) that adjust weighted connections through data.

###Major Types of Neural Networks
* Feedforward Neural Networks (FNN)
To put it simply Feed forward Network is like an asembly line. It is the most basic type of neural network. Where information only moves in one direction, forward. Data enters through an "input layer", passes through one or more "hidden layers" that process the information, and exits as a final decision through an "output layer". Feedforward Neural Network is best fore: Simple tasks like identifying if an email is spam or predicting a price based on a spreadsheet of basic data.
